        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and gait"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Looks well and walks unaided."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cervical examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Tender lower cervical spine and paraspinal muscles, increased trapezius tone, and mildly reduced range of motion in all directions due to pain. No deformity or step."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neurologic examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Power 5/5 throughout with no drift; normal tone; reflexes 2+ and symmetrical with no clonus; sensation intact to light touch and pin; coordination normal on finger-nose-finger and heel-shin testing; normal gait including tandem; Hoffmann and Babinski negative. No objective weakness, focal sensory deficit, or signs of cervical myelopathy or focal radiculopathy today."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Motor vehicle accident and emergency department assessment"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Rear-ended approximately 4–5 weeks before this visit. Seen in the emergency department the same day; whiplash recorded, no loss of consciousness, no imaging, cervical spine cleared, and discharged with simple analgesia."
      }
    },
    {
